## Per-connection footprint

`bench-peer-scaling` measures protocol-core bytes per connection (inline state
plus heap) in four states: idle, after a first message warms the read path
(the checked ~2 KiB budget), with sixteen calls in flight, and as a loop-hosted
connection that also carries a vat. It then extrapolates each to half a million
sessions. That arithmetic is in-process core memory, not a node holding that
many live sockets. Measure: `zig build bench-peer-scaling -Doptimize=ReleaseFast`.

```=html
